  "text": "Allergies:\nSulfa (Sulfonamide Antibiotics)\n\nChief Complaint:\nfailure to thrive\n\nHistory of Present Illness:\nMs. ___ is a ___ who presented initially to ___ with \nepigastric pain, found on imaging to have 5cm pancreatic mass, \nestablished care with Dr. ___ in pancreatic clinic today, \nadmitted from clinic with failure to thrive for expedited \nwork-up. Pt initially presented to PCP ___ ___ with 2 weeks of \nepigastric pain, poor PO intake, and unintentional 10lb weight \nloss. She was evaluated with an abdominal US which showed 4cm \npancreatic head mass, c/f malignancy. She presented then to \n___ on ___ with severe abdominal pain. There, she was \nevaluated with a CT scan which showed 5.5 x 6.5 x 8cm mass in \nhead of the pancreas, involving duodenal C loop with significant \nRP adenopathy. Herexam in the ED was also suspicious for a \nVirchow's Node. Labs at ___ notable for:- Hgb 12.4, WBC 14.3, \nPlt 333- Na 139, K 3.5, Cl 99, CO2 27, BUN 12, Cr 0.6, Glu 112 - \nnegative UA  Patient referred to ___ for work-up, underwent \nEUS on ___ to have 5.3cm x 3.9cm mass in neck of \npancreas adjacent tothe portal vein. FNA/biopsy taken of mass \nand adjacent lymphnodes. Pathology showing necrotic tissue, but \notherwiseinconclusive. Pt was seen in ___ clinic on ___ to \nestablish care. Shereported continued decreased appetite and \nfatigue/weakness. Shedenied fevers, chills, nausea, diarrhea. Pt \nadmitted to OMED forpain management, failure to thrive and for \nexpedited work-up.  On arrival to the floor, patient reports \nconstipation for thepast 5 days and nearly constant epigastric \npain which is relievedby oxycodone. She reports occasionally \nnumbness and tingling ofher bilateral hands. Denies chest pain, \ndyspnea, ___ edema.Daughter does note some change in color of \nskin.\n\nDischarge Diagnosis:\nPRIMARY DIAGNOSIS:\nPancreatic tuberculosis\nFailure to thrive\n\nSECONDARY DIAGNOSES:\nT-wave inversions V1-V3\nGastroesophageal reflux",
